{"jobs": [{"absolute_url": "https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/affirm/jobs/7808142003", "data_compliance": [{"type": "gdpr", "requires_consent": false, "requires_processing_consent": false, "requires_retention_consent": false, "retention_period": null, "demographic_data_consent_applies": false}], "internal_job_id": 5796925003, "location": {"name": "Remote US"}, "metadata": [{"id": 4128552003, "name": "External Department", "value": "Product", "value_type": "single_select"}, {"id": 28890347003, "name": "PERM Job?", "value": false, "value_type": "yes_no"}], "id": 7808142003, "updated_at": "2026-08-12T15:12:11-04:00", "requisition_id": "JR104131", "title": "Chief of Staff Director, Product", "company_name": "Affirm", "first_published": "2026-07-23T15:23:04-04:00", "language": "en", "application_deadline": null, "content": "&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Product team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product team listens to our customers’ needs and translates those insights into a clear product vision. The team works closely with design, engineering, and analytics to build scalable financial products that empower people to manage their money with confidence. We rely on empathy, curiosity, and business sense to prioritize features and improve experiences. Our role is to lead with clarity, support cross-functional execution, and champion the user in every decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Chief of Staff to the SVP of Product is the strategic thought partner and proxy to the leader. The role exists to scale the product leadership function: by anchoring on the leveraged people problems most central to the org, by owning the external product narrative end-to-end, and by being on point for strategic bets that need a single accountable owner (ex: AI enablement, special projects).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The end goal is a healthy Product org with pillar leads running independently at high quality, decisions made with less latency, and a clearer story about where Product is going, and why.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Design and run the product leadership team’s rhythms (staff meetings, product reviews, all-teams, offsites): agenda architecture, pre-reads, decision capture, follow-through&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Co-own the people rhythms with the HRBP across hiring, calibrations, performance, and talent reviews. Surface emergent structural risks (broken hiring funnels, attrition signals, single points of failure) with proactive solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partners with Technology Operations function to define and improve processes for roadmap planning, driving prioritization decisions, setting annual OKRs and tracking progress to goals throughout the year&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own headcount planning and budget management alongside the Finance and HR Business Partners: annual planning, quarterly reforecasts, hire-prioritization tradeoffs&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive AI retooling and enablement, including running internal AI masterclasses for leadership and natively embedding AI-enabled processes across the function&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Curate the external product narrative (all-hands, written updates, major external talks): operate as a speechwriter, partnering with PR, comms, and brand&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prepare executive briefings and leadership communications, and reduce decision latency across the Product leadership team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run a recurring org health pulse (engagement scores, regrettable attrition, leveling drift, manager effectiveness), escalating early signals before they become structural problems&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years in roles that built product credibility and strategic-narrative chops: strategy with deep product partnership, or a prior CoS role to a senior product or engineering executive at a high-growth tech company&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of running people processes at scale (hiring, calibrations, leveling, talent reviews) in a fast-growing organization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exceptional written communication: you can ghostwrite, synthesize narrative from raw inputs, and draft a board page that holds up under scrutiny&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pattern-matching for organizational dysfunction: the muscle to spot a broken hiring funnel, a single point of failure, or a leadership gap before anyone names it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comfort operating with influence and without authority across senior leaders in Product, Engineering, Design, Revenue, Finance, and HR&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong analytical foundation and business acumen: fluent enough in product metrics, financials, and growth analytics to reason about tradeoffs without delegating every quantitative question&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why this role matters&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Affirm’s next phase of growth depends on Product moving from a function powered by heroics to a function powered by a world-class operating system. The Chief of Staff is the linchpin of the strategic side of that change: the partner who helps make the strategy clear, the org stronger, and the leader’s leverage real.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Pay Grade&lt;/strong&gt; - S&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grade&lt;/strong&gt; - USA11&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include equity rewards, monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents.)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (CA, WA, NY, NJ, CT) per year: &lt;span data-formula-id=&quot;_c_f_k_P5xGmz9k_0&quot; data-error=&quot;false&quot; data-placeholder=&quot;false&quot; data-loading=&quot;false&quot; data-recalculating=&quot;false&quot; data-inactive=&quot;false&quot;&gt;$255,000 - $335,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;USA base pay range (all other U.S. states) per year: &lt;span data-formula-id=&quot;_c_f_k_P5xGmz9k_0&quot; data-error=&quot;false&quot; data-placeholder=&quot;false&quot; data-loading=&quot;false&quot; data-recalculating=&quot;false&quot; data-inactive=&quot;false&quot;&gt;$226,000 - $306,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company! The majority of our roles are remote and you can work almost anywhere within the country of employment. Affirmers in proximal roles have the flexibility to work remotely, but will occasionally be required to work out of their assigned Affirm office. A limited number of roles remain office-based due to the nature of their job responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re extremely proud to offer competitive benefits that are anchored to our core value of people come first. Some key highlights of our benefits package include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Health care coverage - Affirm covers all premiums for all levels of coverage for you and your dependents&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Flexible Spending Wallets - generous stipends for spending on Technology, Food, various Lifestyle needs, and family forming expenses&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Time off - competitive vacation and holiday schedules allowing you to take time off to rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;ESPP - An employee stock purchase plan enabling you to buy shares of Affirm at a discount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We believe It’s On Us to provide an inclusive interview experience for all, including people with disabilities. We are happy to provide reasonable accommodations to candidates in need of individualized support during the hiring process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;[For U.S. positions that could be performed in Los Angeles or San Francisco] Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance and Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance, Affirm will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and hereby freely and unambiguously give informed consent to the collection, processing, use, and storage of your personal information as described therein.&lt;/p&gt;
